From 2a9ff82a9109bd5637174404b772c8935c7eb008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:10:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 44/59] feat(vss): one snapshot for a whole multi-folder
 backup, one shadow copy per volume

Sequential multi-folder backups (GUI and CLI) now go through the batch path
with parallel = 1: the snapshot set is taken once for every folder before the
first upload, so the folders are frozen together instead of each at its own
turn. On Windows, paths on the same volume share one shadow copy (they are
frozen at the same instant), like the Linux one-snapshot-per-device change.

Review fixes (Codex): a run cancelled before it starts takes neither the lock
nor a snapshot; when the set cannot be taken (e.g. one volume refuses VSS),
the folders fall back to one snapshot each, one at a time, so those on healthy
volumes are still backed up.
